// ICF codes, Socialstyrelsen inventory to SNOMED CT mappings, codes b6
// Several sources map to the same target; each mapping is its own assertion.
context {
    collection "icf-snomed-ct" version="2026.1"
    source system="ICF" release="2026"
    target system="SNOMED_CT" release="20251130"
}
defaults {
    mappings {
        preference "primary"
        assessment-method "source-default-granularity"
    }
}
mapping "b6.1" source="b6" target="SNOMED_CT:302249008" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b6 SNOMED CT 302249008 = ICF chapter-6 root: GENITOURINARY AND REPRODUCTIVE FUNCTIONS — the
        umbrella chapter spanning urinary excretory (b610), urination (b620), urinary sensations (b630),
        sexual (b640) and genital/reproductive (b640-b679) functions, per WHO ICF chapter structure.
        Target =, active RF2 production 20260701, the direct SNOMED CT function-observable that names the
        combined urological+genital function as a single observable. This is the closest standard
        equivalent to the chapter umbrella; the urinary-only sibling 50741009 covers half the chapter,
        and 118255001 covers the other half, but 302249008 is the only single concept that spans both
        axes. Broader rather than exact: 302249008 is one observable where the ICF chapter bundles
        urinary+genital+reproductive+menstrual as distinct sub-functions; the target is a single
        flattened function name, and SNOMED CT's urogenital function observable does not explicitly name
        the reproductive/menstrual sub-functions, so it stands broader as the single best umbrella. Low
        tier : the closest defensible single-target umbrella for a multi-axis chapter root,
        term-verified active, but a chapter root is inherently coarse and no independent Athena
        crosswalk exists for an ICF chapter-level code.
        """
}
mapping "b610.1" source="b610" target="SNOMED_CT:63911002" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b610 SNOMED CT 63911002 = ICF b610: the body functions of URINARY EXCRETION —, per WHO ICF
        definition, with children b6100 filtration of urine, b6101 collection of urine, b6108/b6109
        residuals. Target =, active RF2 production 20260701, the direct SNOMED CT function-observable that
        names excretion AS A FUNCTION. This is the closest standard equivalent; no dedicated observable
        exists in the mirror (the urinary-specific candidates are 130953005 which is the output-rate
        sub-function, and 55200000 which is the concentration sub-function). Broader rather than exact:
        63911002 is the general excretory function (covers renal AND other excretory pathways) where ICF
        b610 is specifically urinary excretion (filtration + collection of urine); the target fully
        contains the source but adds non-urinary excretory scope. High tier : direct term-and-scope
        match (excretory function = urinary excretory functions), one-level-broader in system scope,
        term-verified active, no independent Athena crosswalk re-verified.
        """
}
mapping "b610-b639.1" source="b610-b639" target="SNOMED_CT:50741009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b610-b639 SNOMED CT 50741009 = ICF b610-b639: the URINARY FUNCTIONS sub-block range of
        chapter 6 — the contiguous span b610 (urinary excretory functions) through b639 (other
        specified/unspecified urinary functions), i.e. all urinary functions (excretion, urination,
        urinary sensations), excluding the genital/reproductive functions b640+. Target =, active RF2
        production 20260701, the direct SNOMED CT function-observable that names urinary-tract function AS
        A FUNCTION. This is the closest standard equivalent; 302249008 is broader (adds genital axis the
        range excludes), and 42111002 is narrower (bladder-only). Broader rather than exact: 50741009 is
        a single flattened urinary-tract-function observable where the range b610-b639 bundles excretion
        + urination + urinary sensation as distinct sub-functions; the target fully contains the urinary
        domain but is one level coarser in granularity. Moderate tier : direct term-and-scope match
        (urinary tract function = urinary functions range), one-level-broader in granularity,
        term-verified active, but a range code is inherently coarse and no independent Athena crosswalk
        re-verified.
        """
}
mapping "b6100.1" source="b6100" target="SNOMED_CT:88024006" relationship=equivalent quality=100 {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b6100 SNOMED CT 88024006 = ICF b6100: the specific body function of FILTRATION OF URINE —,
        per WHO ICF definition (the glomerular ultrafiltration that forms the primary urine). Target =,
        active RF2 production 20260701, the direct SNOMED CT function-observable that names glomerular
        filtration AS A FUNCTION. This is the standard equivalent: ICF b6100 urine filtration IS renal
        glomerular filtration, and 88024006 denotes exactly that function; the sibling 7015005 is the
        fraction-derivative sub-measure and 405004009 is the status framing. Exact match: source
        (filtration of urine by kidneys) and target (glomerular filtration function) denote the same
        physiological function at the same specificity; crosswalk-equivalent term-and-scope match
        verified active in the mirror.
        """
}
mapping "b6101.1" source="b6101" target="SNOMED_CT:33480009" relationship=partial_overlap {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b6101 SNOMED CT 33480009 = ICF b6101: the specific body function of COLLECTION OF URINE —,
        per WHO ICF definition; this spans the renal-pelvis collecting system, ureters AND bladder
        storage. Target =, active RF2 production 20260701, the SNOMED CT function-observable that names
        bladder FILLING/Storage. This is only a partial fit: no single SNOMED CT concept spans the
        renal-pelvis + ureter + bladder collection/storage axis that ICF b6101 names. 33480009 covers
        ONLY the bladder-filling (storage) component of the source; the renal-pelvis/ureter collection
        axis has no dedicated function observable in the mirror. Partial (weak): the target captures one
        slice (bladder storage) of a multi-structure source, recorded to preserve the lead; per the
        broader-vs-partial boundary rule the target does NOT fully contain the source (renal
        pelvis/ureter collection is outside it), so this is partial not broader.
        """
}
assessment "b6108.omop" source="b6108" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
assessment "b6109.omop" source="b6109" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
mapping "b620.1" source="b620" target="SNOMED_CT:364196001" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b620 SNOMED CT 364196001 = ICF b620: the body functions of URINATION —, per WHO ICF
        definition, with children b6200 urination/bladder emptying, b6201 frequency of urination, b6202
        urinary continence, b6208/b6209 residuals. Target =, active RF2 production 20260701, the SNOMED CT
        observable that names the general micturition/urination characteristic. This is the closest
        standard equivalent: the direct SNOMED CT 364196001 28278009 is INACTIVE (retired 2017-01-31) and
        was rejected; 364196001 is the active umbrella micturition-feature observable whose children
        include 364197005, 364198000, 364199008. Broader rather than exact: ICF b620 is a multi-child
        function block (b6200-b6209) bundling voiding, frequency AND continence where 364196001 is a
        single micturition-feature observable; the target names the central act-family but does not
        subsume the continence sub-function (which maps to its own target 405002008). High tier : direct
        term-and-scope match (micturition feature = urination functions), one-level-broader in
        granularity, term-verified active, no independent Athena crosswalk re-verified.
        """
}
